  nonce: 228a  # 228a
  message: "PR #51 (dev d43bd4056d): fixed. The __init__ own-field scan now normalizes ast.Assign and ast.AnnAssign to a common (targets, value) shape, so an annotated self.x: T = v own field is captured into meta['fields'] + own_field_names (previously only plain Assign was scanned, leaving an annotated own field eligible for a confidently-wrong Site-3 hint to a same-named parent field). Evidence: test_annassign_self_field_captured (self.x: Foo = x -> meta['fields']=={'x':'Foo'}); full slice green, 100% cov. Scope = Issue 1 (AnnAssign). Issue 2 (same-name-class short-name clobber in the meta['fields'] attach) remains the deferred id-keyed follow-up documented in-code; needs a class_symbol_by_node_id map + re-keying the name-keyed consumer dicts."  # 228a
